==Ancient Greek==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|grc|κλέϝος||pho}}

===Etymology===
{{root|grc|ine-pro|*klew-}}
From {{inh|grc|grk-pro|*kléwos}} (whence {{cog|gmy|𐀐𐀩𐀺}}), from {{inh|grc|ine-pro|*ḱléwos}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|श्रवस्|tr=śrávas|sc=Deva}}, {{cog|ae|𐬵𐬀𐬬𐬀𐬭𐬯}}, {{cog|xcl|լու|}}, {{m|xcl|լսեմ}}, {{cog|cu|колено}}, {{cog|sga|clú}}, {{cog|cy|clywed}}. Compare {{m|grc|κλύω||I hear}} and {{m|grc|κλέω}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{grc-noun|*κλέεος|n|third}}

# [[rumour]], [[report]]
# good report, [[fame]], [[glory]]
# {{lb|grc|rare}} bad report, [[disrepute]]

====Inflection====
{{rfinfl|grc|noun}}
Only used in the nominative and accusative singular {{m|grc|κλέος}} and the {{grc-epi}} nominative plural {{m|grc|κλέᾰ}}, {{m|grc|κλεῖᾰ}}.

